ium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 100,\n      \"summary\": \"Taking over a dead release claim uses PublishFile with ExpectDigest, whose check followed by rename is not an atomic compare-and-swap. Two concurrent cancels can both replace the stale claim and enter the release body, recording duplicate failed runs and racing for the single receipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 177,\n      \"summary\": \"recordedAbandonmentRun discards ReadReviewRuns' non-fatal loss list, and orphanReservations likewise discards run-history losses. If a prior abandonment run is unreadable, recovery treats it as absent and may write a duplicate run instead of failing closed on unknown history.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:76-103,155-166 adds owner-aware takeover and run reuse, but pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1126-1149 does not route retries once LatestRun is set; delegation_release_test.go:263-303 calls the Store directly\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:123-126,153 requires explicit confirmation and records it; delegation_release_test.go:338-348\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:233-249; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go:192-195; delegation_release_test.go:352-365\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the complete round-4 change and supporting lifecycle code: CLI flag parsing/help and cancel routing, release claim acquisition/takeover, run and receipt recovery, reservation/run/receipt loss handling, attempt listing and ledger admission, reaper and dispatch code, brief/template digest, English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies, plus focused regression tests.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5b33543f852b4244\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I verified marker and process-identity handling, the dead-owner check for marked attempts, and the explicit confirmation required for older markerless reservations. L1-L3 remain stated technical residuals; L4 is an accepted operator-confirmation risk, recorded in the failed run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Initial claims are exclusive, but stale-claim takeover uses a non-atomic expected-bytes replacement with no coordinating lock.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI adds an optional confirmation flag and keeps the existing run and receipt schemas; attempt listing and dispatch integration remain present.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The release recovery path treats an incomplete run-history read as if no matching abandonment run exists.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The delegation lifecycle surface remains integrated; focused CLI and pose tests pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A run-history loss is not surfaced by the recovery helper before it writes another run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I examined the serialized attempt, failed run and receipt fields; no schema change is introduced, and the new flag is optional.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The Store can reuse an already-recorded abandonment run, but the CLI cannot reach that recovery path once the run is visible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D2's owner-aware claim is intended to serialize recovery. The dead-owner takeover path instead uses a check-then-rename publication without a lock, so concurrent retries can both proceed. The sealed structural assessment reports no deltas.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I compared the English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies: they describe Linux reaping, the confirmation required for markerless attempts, and takeover of interrupted releases. The brief template remains versioned and digested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"After an interrupted release has written its run, cancel reports that the stalled attempt is not running and provides no route to complete its missing receipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The release retry can remain blocked after its run was recorded but before its receipt was published.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5b33543f852b4244\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The changes remain within the approved reaping, release recovery, CLI/help, brief, tests and documentation scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reaper still matches the run's sealed-checkout marker and pins processes before signaling; markerless release requires explicit operator confirmation and records that authority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An owner-bearing claim is a small recovery design, but the smallest sufficient implementation needs atomic exclusive takeover or a coordinating lock; the current compare-then-rename permits concurrent release bodies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully; it reported repository-wide orphan provenance warnings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5b33543f852b4244\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the JSON design assessment; the sealed digest matches and it reported no structural deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully without persistence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the non-persisting assessment; its generic unobserved HTTP consumer gaps do not overlap the scoped delegation change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran; the report noted two unrelated invalid spec inputs and an incomplete scan.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, so it cannot pass before attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, so it cannot pass before attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required surface check ran with zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict rerun was blocked before checks because the read-only sandbox could not create Go build directories; sealed build evidence and focused tests cover the implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict module rerun was blocked by the same read-only Go build-directory limitation; sealed pose-mcp build evidence and focused tests cover the code.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
